Mutation
- [N16] Node-level mutation: element=guard(b1,n4,"v1 = 'Yes'") -> guard(b3,n8,"v3 = 'Yes'") -> guard(b5,n13,"v5 = 'Yes'"); source=i3:If the login is successful,; reason=The guards abstract the qualitative condition 'login is successful' into an exact equality check against an invented variable and value ('Yes').
- [N17] Node-level mutation: element=guard(b1,n5,"v1 = 'No'") -> guard(b3,n9,"v3 = 'No'") -> guard(b5,n15,"v5 = 'No'"); source=i5:However, if the login fails,; reason=The guards distort the 'login fails' condition into an exact equality check against an invented value ('No').
- [N18] Node-level mutation: element=guard(b2,n6,"v2 = 'Yes'"); source=i6:If you want to try again,; reason=The guard distorts the retry condition by converting it into a variable equality check ('Yes').
